From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:52:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-129: WinForms' / BCB6's Format menu -- Align to
 Grid, Size to Grid, spacing Increase / Decrease / Remove, Lock All (0.129.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From the manuals check (EastSun 20261001; the users come from C++Builder 6): the Format menu had
only Make Equal spacing.
- 對齊格線 / 大小對齊格線 (Align to Grid / Size to Grid): every selected one's left / top or width /
  height onto GRID.size (default 8) -- old pages have many places that are not multiples of 8
- 水平 / 垂直間距 加大 / 縮小 / 移除 (VBA forms designer: "Increase, to increase the space between
  controls by one grid block"; "Remove ... immediately adjacent"; "The object with focus does not
  move"): the primary stays, the k-th one away moves k gaps' worth; Decrease never past touching
- 全部鎖定 (Lock Controls), the pair of 全部解除鎖定: every component right under the form (so all
  inside them); the form itself is never locked here
Each = one Ctrl+Z; a locked one does not move, said.
Tests: probe (to grid = multiples of 8; Increase = the other moved 8 px, the primary not; Remove =
side by side); smoke (lock all = Panel1 / GroupBox1 / GroupBox2 / Panel2, spbSave counts as locked,
not the form; unlock all frees them). run_all 3/3 layers (lib 168, smoke 201).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
